  <content>
  <section><title>Activity</title>
<para>Your teacher will give your group three different kinds of balls.</para>
<para>Your goal is to measure the rebound heights, model the relationship between the number of bounces and the heights,
  and compare the bounciness of the balls.</para>
<para><figure><media alt="Group of different types of sport balls."><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/7aad8ac5fcd4bb04314b4fda7c3e695d94198cb1"/></media></figure></para>
<example><exercise>
  <problem>
    
    <para>Create a table similar to the one below and begin your investigation. Make sure to note which ball goes with
        which column. </para>
    <table class="os-raise-wideequaltable">
      <thead>
        <row>
          <entry scope="col" class="emphasis">\(n\), Number of Bounces</entry>
          <entry scope="col" class="emphasis">\(a\), Height for Ball 1 (cm)</entry>
          <entry scope="col" class="emphasis">\(b\), Height for Ball 2 (cm)</entry>
          <entry scope="col" class="emphasis">\(c\), Height for Ball 3 (cm)</entry>
        </row>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <row>
          <entry>
            0
          </entry>
